{
  "id": "calc3.multiple_integrals.polar-quarter-disk",
  "course": "calc3",
  "topic": "multiple_integrals",
  "kind": "integral_setup",
  "title": "Convert to polar: a quarter disk",
  "prompt": "Convert $\\displaystyle\\int_0^1 \\int_0^{\\sqrt{1 - x^2}} (x^2 + y^2)\\,dy\\,dx$ to polar coordinates, integrating $dr$ first, then $d\\theta$ (don't evaluate).",
  "answer_format": "An iterated integral like int(int(f, y, a, b), x, c, d), inner integral first. Don't evaluate it. Use r and theta.",
  "difficulty": 2,
  "tags": [
    "double integrals",
    "polar coordinates"
  ],
  "data": {
    "integrand": "x^2 + y^2",
    "region": [
      [
        "y",
        "0",
        "sqrt(1 - x^2)"
      ],
      [
        "x",
        "0",
        "1"
      ]
    ],
    "order": [
      "r",
      "theta"
    ],
    "coordinates": "polar"
  },
  "answer": "int(int(r^3, r, 0, 1), theta, 0, pi/2)",
  "mistakes": [],
  "hints": [
    "The region is the part of the unit disk in the first quadrant.",
    "x² + y² = r², and dA = r dr dθ."
  ],
  "solution": [
    "The region is the quarter disk $0 \\le r \\le 1$, $0 \\le \\theta \\le \\frac{\\pi}{2}$.",
    "$x^2 + y^2 = r^2$ and $dA = r\\,dr\\,d\\theta$, so the integral is $\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\int_0^1 r^2\\cdot r\\,dr\\,d\\theta$."
  ],
  "reference": {
    "book": "openstax-calc3",
    "section": "5.3 Double Integrals in Polar Coordinates",
    "note": "Original problem."
  },
  "review": {
    "status": "draft"
  },
  "examples": [
    {
      "name": "polar with Jacobian",
      "submission": {
        "steps": [],
        "answer": "int(int(r^2 * r, r, 0, 1), theta, 0, pi/2)"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": "correct"
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "forgot the extra r",
      "submission": {
        "steps": [],
        "answer": "int(int(r^2, r, 0, 1), theta, 0, pi/2)"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": "incorrect",
        "hint_codes": [
          "MISSING_JACOBIAN"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "half disk instead of a quarter",
      "submission": {
        "steps": [],
        "answer": "int(int(r^3, r, 0, 1), theta, 0, pi)"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": "incorrect",
        "hint_codes": [
          "REGION_MISMATCH"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "integrand still in x and y",
      "submission": {
        "steps": [],
        "answer": "int(int((x^2 + y^2) r, r, 0, 1), theta, 0, pi/2)"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": "incorrect",
        "hint_codes": [
          "INTEGRAND_NOT_CONVERTED"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "name": "cartesian answer",
      "submission": {
        "steps": [],
        "answer": "int(int(x^2 + y^2, y, 0, sqrt(1 - x^2)), x, 0, 1)"
      },
      "expect": {
        "status": "incorrect",
        "hint_codes": [
          "WRONG_COORDINATES"
        ]
      }
    }
  ]
}
